  "answer": "Absent signed custom terms, NovaLearn’s standard policy states that “standard deletion is executed within 90 days after contract termination” [NL-007#NL-007-S06]. That corresponds to a 30-day suspension window, followed by deletion of active databases, vector indexes, and file stores completed within 60 days of suspension (90 days total from contract termination) [NL-007#NL-007-S06]. The workflow places backup invalidation/cryptographic erasure on days 61–90 and compliance sign-off on Day 91 [NL-007#NL-007-S06]. Separately, the same policy says cold-storage backups are deleted per the 30-day backup rotation cycle, “ensuring full cryptographic erasure within 120 days of contract termination” [NL-007#NL-007-S06]. So, under the standard timeline, operational tenant-data decommissioning is completed within 90 days; if “complete” includes full cold-storage cryptographic erasure, the stated outer bound is 120 days [NL-007#NL-007-S06]. This is consistent with the security discussion describing physical deletion from primary storage and secure backups as taking up to 90 days [NL-019#NL-019-S05].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer  \nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
